course: dictionary
lesson: 2007
title: Learning a word from its context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A concussion is a brain injury caused by a hard knock to the head. You may not know the word, but the sentences around it give you clues. «A head that hits the ground can cause a concussion, an injury to the brain that needs a doctor.» The words after the comma explain the word: an injury to the brain.
explain: Look for clue words like «that is», «like» and «or», which often explain a word. «Your brain floats inside your skull, and a hard knock, like a tackle in rugby, can shake it: that is concussion.» The phrase «that is concussion» tells you the meaning straight away.
explain: Think about what happens around the word. «A boy kept leaning back on two legs of his chair; it slid out and he cracked the back of his head on the floor.» The knock to the head is the clue that leads to concussion. Always check your guess by putting it into the sentence.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A concussion is a brain injury caused by a hard knock to the head.
fact: Signs of concussion include feeling dizzy, sick, confused or sleepy, or having a headache.
fact: In sport, a player who hits their head must stop playing and be checked by an adult or doctor.
fact: «If in doubt, sit them out» is a safety rule: when you are not sure, take the player off.
exercise: What does concussion mean? | A cut on the knee from a fall | *A brain injury caused by a hard knock to the head | A bruise on the arm from a bump | A cold that makes you sneeze
exercise: A player hits their head in a football match. What should happen? | They take off their helmet and carry on | They keep playing until the whistle | *They stop playing and are checked by an adult or doctor | They run faster to win the game
exercise: Which of these is a sign of concussion? | *Feeling dizzy and confused | Wanting to dance around the room | Feeling hungry after lunch | Having cold hands on a winter morning
test: «Your brain floats inside your skull, and a hard knock can shake it: that is concussion.» Which words tell you what concussion is? | Your brain floats | inside your skull | like a tackle in rugby | *a hard knock can shake it
test: Why do cyclists and skaters wear helmets? | *To protect the head from a hard knock that could cause concussion | To keep their hair dry in the rain | To look cool when they ride | To make the bike go faster
exam: Mia's friend hits her head hard in netball and then feels dizzy and sleepy. What should Mia do? | Wait until the end of the match to mention it | Keep playing, because dizziness goes away by itself | *Tell an adult straight away so her friend stops playing and can be checked | Give her a drink and let her run on
